            <ArticleTitle>Occupational hazard for pathologists: microscope use and musculoskeletal disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>543-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1309/AJCPUXDS5KJKRFVW</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The association of prolonged microscope use with the development of chronic pain syndromes has been recognized for nearly 3 decades; yet most pathologists are not well-informed about this hazard until after they develop a problem. The purpose of this article is to make pathologists aware of this risk, discuss current pathogenetic models, and encourage them to proactively integrate prevention strategies into their daily lives.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
